{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2900","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2900","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2900\",\"parent_revision\":\"da2d90d305c0f3e91dbdd8e7d92434457b74d49e\",\"root_revision\":\"ec58be3a8c2ea71b680b9871bc9654a48db625b6e2929d32da0543f08cc3c6c0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nObserved during /dh:work-backlog-item --auto grooming of item #983 (2026-08-16). backlog view --selector \\\"#983\\\" and backlog update --selector \\\"#983\\\" --status \\\"in-progress\\\" both succeed and correctly resolve the item. But backlog groom --selector \\\"#983\\\" --section \\\"RT-ICA\\\" --content \\\"...\\\" (with and without --repo Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills) raises:\\n\\nBacklogError: Item has no backend reference\\n  at backlog_core/operations.py:3164 _apply_groomed_update -> \\\"if not item.reference: raise BacklogError(...)\\\"\\n\\nReproduced with selector as \\\"#983\\\", \\\"983\\\" (bare number), and the full title string \u2014 same failure every time, so this is not a selector-parsing issue upstream; item.reference is genuinely unset on the resolved item object at the point _apply_groomed_update runs, even though the same item resolves fine for view/update. Suggests backlog groom's item-loading path populates a different/incomplete object than backlog view/update use, or the GitHub backend's reference field (likely GraphQL node ID) isn't being carried through whatever load path groom uses.\\n\\nImpact: blocks the entire grooming swarm's finalize.md write step (backlog_groom with mark_groomed=True) and any use of the RT-ICA snapshot write in groom/analyze.md \u2014 i.e. /dh:groom-backlog-item and /dh:work-backlog-item's auto-groom step (Step 3.1) cannot complete grooming on any item via the CLI in this environment. This blocked auto-mode grooming of item #983 and forced a workaround (direct implementation bypassing the SAM grooming/planning pipeline).\\n\\nRepro:\\nuv run sam_schema/cli.py backlog groom --selector \\\"#983\\\" --section \\\"RT-ICA\\\" --content \\\"test\\\"\\n-> BacklogError: Item has no backend reference\\n\\nRelated: #2899 (artifact register/list write-vs-read mismatch) \u2014 filed same session, may share a root cause in how the GitHub backend resolves/persists item references after certain operations.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bug(backlog-mcp): backlog groom fails with backlogerror 'item has no backend reference' for valid open github items** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt-Ica-Probe\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-16T01:03:22.799942Z</sub>\\n\\nverification content\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt-Ica-Probe\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-16T01:03:22.799942Z</sub>\\n\\nverification content\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2edc31c5775ba984ad4086cb316138064c0b712dd4d006d4091a05d513a7f6d1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS_WzA\"}"}